// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #6319 new: Rundll32 Execution of DLL Masquerading as Non-Executable File Type
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6319
// Pull request author: PpT2211
// Change: new rule
// Title: Rundll32 Execution With Module In User-Writable Staging Directory
// Sigma ID: a7e1d2c4-5b38-4f6a-9c0e-2d4b8f1a6e73
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Pavan Pothamsetti (PpT2211)
// Date: 2026-08-28 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1218.011
// Tags: detection.threat-hunting
// Description: Detects rundll32.exe where the module to be loaded (the argument before the first comma) is
//   located in a user-writable staging directory such as Temp, AppData\Roaming, ProgramData,
//   Users\Public or Downloads. Legitimate rundll32 targets normally live under System32 or Program
//   Files. Paths that appear only as arguments to the export function (e.g. the file passed to
//   shell32.dll,OpenAs_RunDLL) are intentionally not matched. Unlike the Qakbot-specific rule, this
//   is not tied to specific parent processes, so it is broader and intended as a hunting/triage
//   signal. Execution with a msiexec.exe parent is excluded.
// False positives:
//   - Browser components, printer/scanner utilities and some updaters load DLLs from AppData or ProgramData during normal operation. Baseline before alerting
// References:
//   - https://www.fortinet.com/blog/threat-research/infostealer-malware-formbook-spread-via-phishing-campaign-part-i
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/afa8c265b64cc6a4c53b6a09aae7a487029c90a0/rules-threat-hunting/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_rundll32_susp_module_staging_dir.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ((FolderPath endswith "\\rundll32.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "RUNDLL32.EXE") and ProcessCommandLine matches regex "(?i)rundll32(\\.exe)?\"?\\s+\"?[^,]*\\\\(AppData\\\\Local\\\\Temp|AppData\\\\Roaming|ProgramData|Users\\\\Public|Downloads)\\\\[^,]*,") and (not(InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\msiexec.exe"))
